A hosted screen draws its conversation before its extensions bind.

pi's startup binds every extension, awaiting each one's session_start in
turn, and only then draws the conversation. On a busy machine a host's
opens spent 48 to 146 s in that bind, most of it in four extensions'
session_start handlers reading shared state off a stalled disk, and the
person's window stayed blank the whole time: nothing on it said which
conversation it was or what had been said.

A hosted screen now starts its bind as a reload already does, with pi's
own renderBeforeBind: it draws the conversation and subscribes to the
agent first, then binds, and skips the draw startup would make after. The
resources pi lists once its extensions bind still land above the
conversation, in their own container; the startup notices a bind adds
come below it, as after a reload. A plain pi starts as before.

Apply only to the host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays
unchanged.

--- a/packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts
@@ -1185,12 +1185,15 @@ export class InteractiveMode {
 		this.setupEditorSubmitHandler();
 		this.ui.requestRender();
 
-		// Initialize extensions first so resources are shown before messages
-		await this.rebindCurrentSession();
+		// Initialize extensions first so resources are shown before messages. A hosted screen draws its
+		// conversation before extensions bind, as a reload does, so a slow session_start leaves it readable;
+		// the resources still land above it, in their own container.
+		const hosted = this.options.hosted !== undefined;
+		await this.rebindCurrentSession({ renderBeforeBind: hosted });
 		if (this.hostedStartupEnded()) return;
 
 		// Render initial messages AFTER showing loaded resources
-		this.renderInitialMessages();
+		if (!hosted) this.renderInitialMessages();
 
